---
title: Gyudon
servings: 1
course: dinner
tags: quick, beef, rice
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/M-PuGg7Ek-w/maxresdefault.jpg
source: https://youtu.be/M-PuGg7Ek-w
time: 15m
---

Bring a small #pot{} of @water to a boil, add @egg{1}, and boil for ~{6%minutes}. Immediately transfer the egg to cold water to stop cooking, then peel and set aside.

In a #saucepan{}, bring @water{120%ml} and @dashi powder{1%packet} to a simmer. Add @mirin{2%tbsp}, @sake{2%tbsp}, and @soy sauce{2%tbsp}. Finely grate in @garlic{1%clove} and @ginger{10%g}, then reduce the heat to low.

Peel and thinly slice @brown onion{1}. Add the onion to the broth and simmer until tender and translucent, about ~{5%minutes}.

Thinly slice @beef steak{200%g} against the grain. Slice @spring onion{2}, separating the white parts and dark green tops.

Add the sliced beef to the simmering broth and onions, stirring gently to poach the meat without boiling it, about ~{2%minutes}. Add a splash of water if dry. Taste and adjust with a pinch of @salt if needed. Stir in most of the spring onions and remove from heat.

Place @cooked white rice{1%bowl} into a serving #bowl{}. Spoon the beef, onions, and broth over the rice. Top with the soft-boiled egg, @pickled ginger{2%tbsp}, reserved spring onion greens, and @sesame seed{1%tsp}.
